I did not make a submission. On September 3, 2026 I served the State of Ore=
gon with a tort claim notice under ORS 30.275, and notice of documented Fir=
st Amendment retaliation supported by the records Oregon State Police produ=
ced that same day under PR27478.
 Those are notices, not a claim application, and the distinction is not cle=
rical. A notice preserves rights. It is not a request that the state evalua=
te anything. Except its conduct.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
<br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
Assigning an adjuster does not respond to what I sent. An adjuster values a=
nd disposes of claims. Nothing I have asked for is within an adjuster's aut=
hority. I have asked the Department, its Director, its Deputy Director, and=
 the Governor's office for an independent
 investigation and for an accounting of what was done and by whom. Those re=
quests remain outstanding and unanswered.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
